SUMMARY:Feelgood
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:Rave / house • Toronto\n\nAaron\, aka Feelgood\, grew up in 
 the Toronto area and is heavily influenced by the rave culture of the lat
 e 90s and early 00s. He has spent a decade organizing and promoting event
 s under the brand Release\, and held multiple weekly residencies for year
 s which helped him develop the ability to play to the crowd.\n\nProfile: 
 https://thenectarfestival.com/products/feelgood
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:7cd2e075-68cb-4d44-a0ed-15b7a7cc0e43@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260619T213000
SUMMARY:Bedtime Snack
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:DnB / Dubstep • Indigenous NW Coast\n\nJayden\, also known a
 s bedtime snack\, is an Indigenous artist from the Kwakwaka’wakw ~ Wuik
 inuxv ~ Tla’amin nations\, deeply rooted in the Northwest Coast of so-c
 alled British Columbia. Whether it’s drum and bass at sunrise or dubste
 p at sundown\, Jayden has a capacity to capture a feeling and share it wi
 th the dancefloor.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/bed
 time-snack
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6ccb1cd0-effe-4ed5-bad3-4baf1fb62a9d@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260620T213000
SUMMARY:Ephemeral Objects & IHA
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:Dub / leftfield / experimental\n\nephemeral objects moves betw
 een ethereal\, dubwise atmospheres\, textural grooves\, and ambient intro
 spection\, with an affinity for deep\, hypnotic\, and experimental sounds
 . Her DJ sets are both meditative and kinetic\, drawing from labels and p
 roducers operating at the fringes of techno\, leftfield bass\, psychedeli
 a\, and downtempo.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/eph
 emeral-objects\n\n— — —\n\nDub / techno / experimental • Vancouve
 r\n\nHailing from the rich musical fabric of Vancouver\, IHA is a produce
 r\, DJ\, sound artist\, and curator behind Naga\, a multimedia label and 
 event platform. Rooted in memory\, dreams\, and shifting perception\, the
 ir sets carry a curious\, instinctive energy — ranging from dubby atmos
 pheres to playful techno and forward-thinking sounds.\n\nProfile: https:/
 /thenectarfestival.com/products/iha
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:5106b8d9-abbb-4622-9b2d-5d51067f5de0@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T190000
SUMMARY:Coco
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:Rap / R&B / eclectic • Salt Spring Island\n\nCoco is a multi
 disciplinary artist from Salt Spring Island with a gift for curating unfo
 rgettable vibes. A DJ\, tattoo artist\, drum maker\, hypnotherapist\, and
  women’s empowerment coach\, she brings depth\, creativity\, and magnet
 ic energy to everything she touches. She plays a spectrum of music includ
 ing rap\, femme rap\, and R&B.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/
 products/coco
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:d2e412f6-0e9e-4d34-85d0-e2f31fbacd3d@nectar2026
DTSTAMP:20260615T233644Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Vancouver:20260621T213000
SUMMARY:Ray Black & Michael Red
LOCATION:Sunset Stage
DESCRIPTION:Future Beats / Wave / Dub • Vancouver\n\nVancouver-based art
 ist Ray Black is an innovative DJ/Vocalist whose work is transforming the
  face of electronic music. Ray takes inspiration from artists within Futu
 re Beats\, Wave\, and Dub\; the result is an ethereal yet hard-hitting so
 und uniquely his own\, taking listeners on a journey at the forefront of 
 the genre.\n\nProfile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/ray-black\n
 \n— — —\n\nProducer / curator • Vancouver (Low Indigo)\n\nMichael
  Red is a Vancouver-based music producer\, film composer\, collaborator\,
  performer and DJ with always a few handfuls of projects on the go. An ac
 tive curator and event producer\, he works with the local underground mus
 ic and creative community in a number of ways\, and is recognized as play
 ing a critical role in the scene. He curates Nectar’s Sunset Stage.\n\n
 Profile: https://thenectarfestival.com/products/michael-red
END:VEVENT
